{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1744167,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"Poster and Paper Presentation","festival_id":504454,"organization_id":675999,"web_url":"www.techfest26.com\/","start_date":"2026-09-02T18:30:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-17T13:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/poster-and-paper-presentation-techfest26-annual-technical-festival-of-sliet-sant-longowal-institute-of-engi-1744167","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>All That You Need to Know About Poster and Paper Presentation &mdash; techFEST'26<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>About techFEST'26<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>techFEST'26 is North India's premier technical festival, organised by Sant Longowal Institute of Engineering and Technology (SLIET), Longowal, Punjab.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Registration for the&nbsp;techFEST&rsquo;26 package&nbsp;is compulsory for&nbsp;accommodation and&nbsp;other perks, while&nbsp;participation in individual&nbsp;events is free*.<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong><a href=\"http:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/\">www.techfest26.com<\/a><\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong>Register Now:<\/strong><br \/><a href=\"https:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/package\">https:\/\/www.techFEST26.com\/package<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>Website and Email:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Website: <a href=\"http:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/\">www.techfest26.com<\/a><\/li>\n<li>Email: <a href=\"mailto:techfest@sliet.ac.in\">techfest@sliet.ac.in<\/a><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Follow us for updates on Instagram and other social media platforms.<\/p>\n<p><strong>For Queries:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Naman Kumar Sinha (Overall Coordinator): +91 78568 93952<\/li>\n<li>Shubham Kumar Singh (Overall Coordinator): +91 97711 74465<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Prepare yourself for a journey of technology, creativity, and celebration.<\/p>\n<p>Mark your calendars and be part of the magic of techFEST'26 at SLIET.<\/p>\n<p>We cordially invite you to Poster and Paper Presentation, organised as part of techFEST'26 &mdash; Annual Technical Festival of SLIET. Showcase your talent, compete with the sharpest minds and earn your moment of glory.<\/p>\n<p><em><strong>&ldquo;Bring your ideas to life on paper and poster boards&rdquo;.<\/strong><\/em><\/p>\n<p><em><strong>About the Event :<\/strong><\/em><\/p>\n<p>It is an event in which participants present their poster and paper presentation.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Details:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Number of Rounds:<\/strong> 3<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Poster Making<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Size of poster should be A1 or A3<\/li>\n<li>Posters can use flow diagrams, newspaper cuttings, etc.<\/li>\n<li>In lieu of physical posters, digital posters will also be accepted<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2: Paper Abstracts<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Format of Abstract:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants: Name, Email, Phone number, College name, Branch, Registration number<\/li>\n<li>Abstract (1&ndash;2 pages): The abstract must have an appropriate title, picture, and overview of the topic<\/li>\n<li>The full paper margin line is 1.5 cm<\/li>\n<li>The abstract must be submitted as a hard copy a week before the presentation<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 3: Presentation<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The presentation must be completed within 7 minutes<\/li>\n<li>Warning bell will be given at 5 minutes<\/li>\n<li>3-minute Question and Answer session<\/li>\n<li>PPT (.pptx file) must be handed to the event coordinator one day before the event<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Judgment Criteria:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Stage 1: Poster &mdash; weightage 30%<\/li>\n<li>Stage 2: Abstract &mdash; weightage 30%<\/li>\n<li>Stage 3: Presentation &mdash; weightage 40%<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Evaluation will be based on:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Creative thinking<\/li>\n<li>Clarity of thoughts<\/li>\n<li>Understanding of the problem statement and proposed solution<\/li>\n<li>Body language and presentation skills<\/li>\n<li>Professionalism in presentation (e.g., communication skills, formal attire)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; FAQ:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All Undergraduate and Diploma students with valid ID cards of their respective educational institutes are allowed to participate<\/li>\n<li>Each participating team may comprise a maximum of 3 members<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the judges will be final and binding<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Certification Policy:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Certificates will be provided to all participants<\/li>\n<li>Certificate of Excellence will be provided to the winners (as per the results declared by the judges)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Important Note:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All the participants must make payment on the techFEST'26 website. Without payment, their participation will not be considered, and they will be disqualified.<\/li>\n<li>The organizers reserve the right to modify the rules, prize pool, dates, venue, or timing of the competition if deemed necessary under unforeseen circumstances.<\/li>\n<li>All guidelines are subject to change. Participants are advised to regularly check the official techFEST'26 website for any updates. Any changes or announcements will be posted there. Adherence to the latest rules is mandatory for all teams.<\/li>\n<li><strong>The details mentioned in this Problem Statement may be subject to change at any time.<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>For Further Query:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Domain Advisor:<\/strong> Sahil Sinha, 2432067\/GCT, 9065297749<\/li>\n<li><strong>Domain Coordinator:<\/strong> Amit Kumar, 254013105\/GCT, 8010064068<\/li>\n<li><strong>Event Coordinator:<\/strong> Karan Singh, 254014021\/GCT, 9277199714<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>General Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All participants must carry a valid college ID card and their techFEST'26 registration receipt.<\/li>\n<li>Reporting time will be communicated to registered teams; late reporting may lead to walkover.<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the judges and organisers will be final and binding in all matters.<\/li>\n<li>Any form of misconduct, plagiarism or use of unfair means leads to immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Participants are responsible for their own equipment and personal belongings.<\/li>\n<li>Organisers reserve the right to modify any rule at any time; updates are announced at the venue.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to students of all institutes and all degree programmes (unless specified otherwise in the event rules above).<\/li>\n<li>Participants must be registered for techFEST'26 through the official portal.<\/li>\n<li>Cross-college teams are welcome.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Mark your calendars and be part of the magic of techFEST'26 at SLIET!<\/p>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":null,"registration_clicks":0,"user_id":27463276,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-08-25T20:40:44+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-01T23:18:20+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"NtpBQ5K","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":1,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":2,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":63,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-08-27 03:52:44","auto_shortlist_trigger":false,"enable_ai_discussion":false,"total_unlock_teams":0,"enable_hiring_automation":false,"auto_send_participation_certificate":false,"closed_at":null,"linkedInE